  lines:
    '|a||A complaint and an apology in Russian: жалоба, извините':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6200
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Complain politely, apologise and ask to be forgiven in Russian: жа́ловаться на, извини́ться пе́ред … за, прости́те нас, and the words of a written apology.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1lu24uk'
    '|a||Февра́ль, ве́чер в «Неве́». Today: a complaint, and an apology.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7440
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Ка́тя, наш администра́тор, прихо́дит ко мне на ку́хню. Послу́шайте.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:aqkunu'
    '|b||Том, клие́нт жа́луется. Он говори́т, что суп был холо́дный.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4240
      voice: 'gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated #ctx:1fooj8i'
    '|a||Холо́дный? Э́то ужа́сно. Я сейча́с сам извиню́сь.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4360
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|b||Он се́рдится, но не кричи́т. Он ве́жливый.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3320
      voice: gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated
    '|a||Принеси́ ему́ горя́чий суп и десе́рт — от нас.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3960
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|b||Хорошо́. А е́сли он напи́шет жа́лобу?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3080
      voice: gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated
    '|a||Тогда́ я отве́чу ему́: прости́те нас. Оши́бку на́до испра́вить.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4560
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|b||Ты прав. Я пойду́.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 1880
      voice: gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated
    '|a||What is the guest complaining about? (клие́нт = a guest; жа́луется = is complaining)':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8880
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Суп был холо́дный.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2160
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Is the guest shouting? (крича́ть = to shout)':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3840
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Не кричи́т. Он ве́жливый.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2760
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||What will Катя bring the guest? (горя́чий = hot)':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4320
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Горя́чий суп и десе́рт — от нас.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3240
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||What will Tom do if the guest writes a complaint (жа́лоба)?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5000
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Отве́чу: прости́те нас.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2760
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Посмотри́те. Клие́нт жа́луется: the guest is complaining.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4240
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Я сам извиню́сь: I''ll apologise myself.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:sot2tv'
    '|a||Прости́те нас: forgive us. Извини́те you know; прости́те often sounds a little stronger.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:noc19a'
    '|a||Но́вые слова́. Клие́нт, a guest or client. Жа́лоба, a complaint. Крича́ть, to shout.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:4czekl'
    '|a||Ве́жливый, polite. Горя́чий, hot. Ужа́сный, terrible: э́то ужа́сно!':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:qe8heu'
    '|a||Испра́вить оши́бку: to put a mistake right.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:12z6i8t'
    '|a||Три сло́ва, и у ка́ждого свой вопро́с.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:104d06n'
    '|a||Жа́ловаться на что: клие́нт жа́луется на суп.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:i3aky0'
    '|a||Я жа́луюсь, ты жа́луешься: like волну́юсь.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:16a5qqn'
    '|a||И кому́: он жа́луется Ка́те.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:pe1qub'
    '|a||Извини́ться пе́ред кем: я извиня́юсь пе́ред ва́ми. Извиня́ться is the other aspect.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1lcb1tg'
    '|a||И за что: за оши́бку, за холо́дный суп.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:129s5is'
    '|a||Прости́ть кого́: прости́те нас. Проща́ть, the other aspect; я прощу́, I''ll forgive.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1o8skvw'
    '|a||Green, the object-case: after на and за, and after прости́ть. Blue, the with-case after пе́ред. Purple, кому́.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1jv0oba'
    '|a||Тепе́рь вы.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 1160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:szuyuk'
    '|a||Вы́берите: на, пе́ред or за.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:l3wk88'
    '|a||Клие́нт жа́луется на холо́дный суп. Том извиня́ется пе́ред клие́нтом за оши́бку. Молоде́ц!':
